@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`

-- ca-tests-counting.l4
--
-- Section 27: clear days, days between events, and the words that tie a time to a day; section 28 and 37(1) refusals;
-- the number of days in a period.  Expected values written from the text before the module was run.

GIVEN p IS A `A period`
      a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
p `runs from` a `to` b MEANS
        (p's `the first day`) EQUALS a
    AND (p's `the last day`) EQUALS b

§ `Weeks: the Act has no provision`

-- The word "week" does not occur in the text, so no function answers and each says so.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 1 `weeks after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 2 `weeks from` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 1 `weeks before` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 52 `weeks after` (YMD 2024 2 29))

§ `A count that is not a whole number of at least one: the Act gives no rule`

#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `months after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `years after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `days before` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `months before` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0 `years before` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` (0 MINUS 3) `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` (0 MINUS 3) `months after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` (0 MINUS 1) `years after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 1.5 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 1.5 `months after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the period of` 0.5 `years from` (YMD 2026 1 1))

§ `Section 27(1): clear days, and "at least" a number of days between two events`

-- Both event days are excluded: between 1 March and 10 March there are the days 2 to 9, which is 8.
#ASSERT `the number of clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 8
-- Two events on consecutive days have no clear day between them.
#ASSERT `the number of clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS 0
-- Across a month end and a year end.
#ASSERT `the number of clear days between` (YMD 2025 12 30) `and` (YMD 2026 1 2) EQUALS 2
-- "at least" three clear days: 2, 3 and 4 March are clear if the second event is on 5 March.
#ASSERT `there are at least` 3 `clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`there are at least` 3 `clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 4))
#ASSERT `there are at least` 3 `clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 10)
-- The earliest day for the second event is the first day after the clear days.
#ASSERT `the earliest day of the second event, if at least` 3 `clear days must lie between it and the first event on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 5
#ASSERT `the earliest day of the second event, if at least` 1 `clear days must lie between it and the first event on` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- Events on one day, or in the wrong order, are not counted by the Act.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the number of clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the number of clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 10) `and` (YMD 2026 3 1))

§ `Section 27(2): a number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between two events`

-- The first event's day is excluded and the second's included: 2 to 10 March is 9 days.
#ASSERT `the number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between` (YMD 2025 12 31) `and` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1
-- If n such days lie between the events, the second event is on the day n after the first.
#ASSERT `the day of the second event, if` 9 `days not expressed to be clear days lie between it and the first event on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the number of days, not expressed to be clear days, between` (YMD 2026 3 10) `and` (YMD 2026 3 1))

§ `Section 27(3), (4) and (5): the word that ties a time to a day`

-- (3): "begin or end at, on or with a specified day, or ... continue to or until" it: the day is included.
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `begins at` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `begins on` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `begins with` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `ends at` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `ends on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `ends with` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `continues to` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `continues until` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
-- (4): "begin after or ... be from a specified day": the day is not included.
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `begins after` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `is from` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `begins after` (YMD 2026 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the first day of a time bounded at its start by` `is from` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- (5): "within a time after, from, of or before a specified day, the time does not include that day".
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `is done before` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
#ASSERT `the last day of a time bounded at its end by` `is done before` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

-- Whole times bounded at both ends, and the number of days each holds (both ends inside).
#ASSERT (`the time bounded by` `begins at` (YMD 2026 3 1) `ends on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the time bounded by` `begins at` (YMD 2026 3 1) `ends on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the time bounded by` `begins after` (YMD 2026 3 1) `continues until` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 3 2) `to` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the time bounded by` `begins after` (YMD 2026 3 1) `continues until` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT (`the time bounded by` `is from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is done before` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `runs from` (YMD 2026 3 2) `to` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the time bounded by` `is from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `is done before` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the time bounded by` `begins with` (YMD 2026 3 5) `ends with` (YMD 2026 3 5)) EQUALS 1

§ `The number of days in a period`

#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 30 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2024 1 31)) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the period of` 4 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29)) EQUALS 1461

§ `Whether a date falls inside a period: the boundaries on each side`

-- The period of one day after 1 January 2026 is the single day 2 January.
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2026 1 1) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
#ASSERT (YMD 2026 1 2) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2026 1 3) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `days after` (YMD 2026 1 1)))
-- A period of one month: 1 to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2025 1 31) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31)))
#ASSERT (YMD 2025 2 1) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT (YMD 2025 2 28) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2025 3 1) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31)))
-- A period of one year: 1 March 2024 to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2024 2 29) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29)))
#ASSERT (YMD 2024 3 1) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29))
#ASSERT (YMD 2025 2 28) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29))
#ASSERT NOT ((YMD 2025 3 1) `falls inside` (`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29)))

§ `What the Act does not define: week, service and notice`

-- The word "week" does not occur in the text: no number of days is said to make one.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the number of days in a week according to the Act`
-- Nothing in the text deems a document served, or a notice given or received, on any day.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day a document is deemed served, if it was sent on` (YMD 2026 3 10))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the day a notice is deemed received, if it was given on` (YMD 2026 3 10))
